<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew – Introduction</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">עַל-פִּי הַמַּאֲמָר "לַשֶּׁמֶשׁ שָׂם אֹהֶל בָּהֶם" וְכוּ' בְּסִימָן מט, עַיֵּן שָׁם כָּל הַמַּאֲמָר כֻּלּוֹ: וְהַכְּלָל בְּקִצּוּר, כִּי לְפִי אוֹר לֶהָבִיּוּת הַלֵּב שֶׁל אִישׁ הַיִּשְׂרְאֵלִי אִי אֶפְשָׁר לְהִתְגַּלּוֹת מֵהַמִּדּוֹת, כִּי אוֹר לֶהָבִיּוּתוֹ הוּא עַד אֵין סוֹף וְאֵין תַּכְלִית לִתְשׁוּקָתוֹ וְצָרִיךְ לְצַמְצֵם הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת כְּדֵי שֶׁיִּשָּׁאֵר בַּלֵּב חָלָל, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, וְלִבִּי חָלָל בְּקִרְבִּי. וְעַל-יְדֵי הַצִּמְצוּם שֶׁל הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת יוּכַל לָבֹא לְהִתְגַּלּוּת מֵהַמִּדּוֹת, הַיְנוּ לַעֲבֹד אֶת ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בְּהַדְרָגָה וּבְמִדָּה וְכוּ'. וְעַל-יְדֵי פְּעֻלּוֹתָיו וּמִדּוֹתָיו הַטּוֹבִים יִתְגַּלֶּה, שֶׁהוּא מְקַבֵּל עֹל מַלְכוּת שָׁמַיִם שְׁלֵמָה וְכוּ'. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת בְּרִיאַת הָעוֹלָמוֹת, כִּי קֹדֶם הַבְּרִיאָה הָיָה אוֹר הַקָּדוֹשׁ-בָּרוּךְ-הוּא אֵין סוֹף וְרָצָה הַקָּדוֹשׁ-בָּרוּךְ-הוּא שֶׁיִּתְגַּלֶּה מַלְכוּתוֹ וְכוּ'. וְצִמְצֵם אֶת הָאוֹר אֵין סוֹף לַצְּדָדִין וְנִשְׁאַר חָלָל פָּנוּי. וּבְתוֹךְ הֶחָלָל הַפָּנוּי בָּרָא הָעוֹלָמוֹת וְהֵן הֵן מִדּוֹתָיו וְכוּ' וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נִתְגַּלָּה מַלְכוּתוֹ שֶׁזֶּה עִקַּר כַּוָּנַת הַבְּרִיאָה וְכוּ'. וְזֶהוּ מַמָּשׁ בְּחִינָה הַנַּ"ל, כִּי כְּמוֹ כֵן הוּא בְּכָל אָדָם, שֶׁקֹּדֶם שֶׁזּוֹכֶה לַעֲבוֹדַת ה' בֶּאֱמֶת אֲזַי בִּתְחִלָּה לִבּוֹ כּוֹסֵף וּבוֹעֵר מְאֹד לַה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בְּהִתְלַהֲבוּת גָּדוֹל. וְאוֹר הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת הַזֹּאת שֶׁבַּלֵּב הוּא בְּחִינַת אֵין סוֹף, כִּי אֵין סוֹף וְאֵין תַּכְלִית לִתְשׁוּקָתוֹ וְאַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁלִּבּוֹ מִתְלַהֵב מְאֹד לַה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בֶּאֱמֶת, אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן אֵין זֶה תַּכְלִית, כִּי מִגֹּדֶל הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת הַזֹּאת אֵינוֹ יָכוֹל לַעֲבֹד אֶת ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ כְּלָל מֵעֹצֶם הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת בְּלִבּוֹ עַד אֵין סוֹף. עַד שֶׁאֵינוֹ יָכוֹל לַעֲשׂוֹת שׁוּם מִדָּה טוֹבָה וְשׁוּם עֲבוֹדָה, עַל-כֵּן צָרִיךְ לְצַמְצֵם הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת הַזֹּאת וְלַעֲשׂוֹת חָלָל בַּלֵּב. בְּחִינַת וְלִבִּי חָלָל בְּקִרְבִּי, הַיְנוּ לַעֲשׂוֹת חָלָל בְּאוֹר הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת שֶׁבַּלֵּב, עַל-יְדֵי צִמְצוּם הָאוֹר לַצְּדָדִין, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁמֻּכְרָחִין לְצַמְצֵם הַהִתְלַהֲבוּת הַגָּדוֹל שֶׁבַּלֵּב הַנַּ"ל וַאֲזַי נַעֲשֶׂה חָלָל בַּלֵּב וְשָׁם בְּאוֹתוֹ הֶחָלָל שֶׁבַּלֵּב שֶׁהוּא בְּחִינַת חָלָל הַפָּנוּי. שָׁם מִתְגַּלִּין פְּעֻלּוֹתָיו וּמִדּוֹתָיו הַטּוֹבִים, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי הַצִּמְצוּם הַנַּ"ל, עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה יָכוֹל לַעֲבֹד אֶת ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ בְּהַדְרָגָה וּבְמִדָּה. וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נִתְגַּלֶּה שֶׁהוּא מְקַבֵּל עֹל מַלְכוּת שָׁמַיִם שְׁלֵמָה, שֶׁזֶּה בְּחִינַת הִתְגַּלּוּת מַלְכוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ, שֶׁהוּא תַּכְלִית בְּרִיאָה וְכוּ' וְעַיֵּן שָׁם בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ"ל וְהָבֵן הֵיטֵב הֵיטֵב. כִּי הֵם דְּבָרִים עֲמֻקִּים מְאֹד מְאֹד עָמֹק עָמֹק מִי יִמְצָאֵם. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת תְּשׁוּבָה וְכוּ' וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם:</div>

<p class="first">Based on the discourse <span class="verse-inline">"He placed a tent for the sun among them"</span> etc. in Torah 49 <span class="added">[of Likutay Moharan]</span> — see there the entire discourse. And the principle, in brief: that according to the fiery light of the heart of the Jewish person, it is impossible for the <span class="key-term">midos</span> <span class="added">[attributes/character traits]</span> to be revealed — for the fiery light of his heart is without end and without limit to his longing. And one must contract the <em>hislahavus</em> <span class="added">[fervent enthusiasm]</span> so that there should remain in the heart a <span class="key-term">chalal</span> <span class="added">[hollow space]</span>, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"And my heart is hollow within me"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 109:22)</span>. And through the contraction of the <em>hislahavus</em>, one can come to the revelation of the <em>midos</em> — that is, to serve Hashem in gradual stages and in measured proportion, etc.</p>

<p>And through his good actions and <em>midos</em>, it is revealed that he accepts the complete yoke of the Kingdom of Heaven, etc. And this is the aspect of the <strong>creation of the worlds</strong>. For before creation, the light of the Holy One, blessed be He, was <span class="key-term">Ain Sof</span> <span class="added">[infinite]</span>. And the Holy One, blessed be He, desired that His kingship should be revealed, etc. And He contracted the <em>or Ain Sof</em> <span class="added">[infinite light]</span> to the sides, and there remained a <span class="key-term">chalal panui</span> <span class="added">[vacant space]</span>. And within the vacant space He created the worlds, and they are His <em>midos</em>, etc. And through this, His kingship was revealed — and this is the primary purpose of creation, etc.</p>

<p>And this is precisely the aforementioned aspect. For so it is with every person: before he merits true service of Hashem, initially his heart yearns and burns intensely for Hashem with great <em>hislahavus</em>. And the light of this <em>hislahavus</em> in the heart is the aspect of <em>ain sof</em>, for there is no end and no limit to his longing. And even though his heart burns greatly for Hashem in truth, nevertheless this is not the <em>tachlis</em> <span class="added">[ultimate purpose]</span>. For from the greatness of this <em>hislahavus</em> he cannot serve Hashem at all, due to the intensity of the <em>hislahavus</em> in his heart without end — to the point that he cannot do any good <em>midah</em> or any <em>avodah</em>. Therefore, one must contract this <em>hislahavus</em> and make a <em>chalal</em> in the heart — the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"and my heart is hollow within me"</span> — that is, to make a hollow space in the fiery light in the heart, through contracting the light to the sides. That is, one is compelled to contract the great <em>hislahavus</em> in the heart, and then a hollow space is made in the heart. And there, in that hollow of the heart, which is the aspect of the <em>chalal panui</em> — there his good actions and <em>midos</em> are revealed. For through the aforementioned <em>tzimtzum</em> <span class="added">[contraction]</span>, through this he can serve Hashem in gradual stages and in measured proportion. And through this it is revealed that he accepts the complete yoke of the Kingdom of Heaven — which is the aspect of the revelation of His kingship, blessed be He, which is the ultimate purpose of creation, etc. See there in the aforementioned discourse and understand very, very well. For these are exceedingly deep matters — <span class="verse-inline">"deep, deep — who can find them?"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:24)</span>. And this is the aspect of <em>teshuvah</em>, etc.; see there.</p>

