<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת חֵטְא אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן. שֶׁעִקַּר הַחֵטְא הָיָה עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי הָאוֹר שֶׁגּוֹרֵם שְׁבִירַת כֵּלִים חַס וְשָׁלוֹם, וְעַל-כֵּן הַתְחָלַת עֲצַת הַנָּחָשׁ הָיָה עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה שֶׁבָּא אֶל חַוָּה וְאָמַר לָהּ, אַף כִּי אָמַר אֱלֹקִים לֹא תֹאכְלוּ מִכָּל עֵץ הַגָּן. שֶׁרָצָה לְהַטְעוֹתָהּ עַל-יְדֵי הַמִּצְוֹת שֶׁל הַיֵּצֶר הָרָע וְשָׁאַל אוֹתָהּ, אִם צַוָּאַת ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ הָיָה לִבְלִי לֶאֱכֹל מִכָּל עֵץ הַגָּן, כִּי בְּוַדַּאי כָּךְ רָאוּי לָכֶם לִבְלִי לֶאֱכֹל לְפִי גֹּדֶל עֹצֶם גְּדֻלָּתוֹ וְרוֹמְמוּתוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ, וְאֵיךְ אֶפְשָׁר לָכֶם לֶאֱכֹל כְּלָל שׁוּם דָּבָר?! וּמֵחֲמַת שֶׁהִכְנִיס בָּהֶם סְפֵקוֹת כָּאֵלֶּה, שֶׁרָאוּי הָיָה לִבְלִי לֶאֱכֹל כְּלָל, אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁלֹּא פָּעַל כָּל רְצוֹנוֹ, אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן פָּעַל קְצָת שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הֵשִׁיבָה חַוָּה לוֹ בְּטָעוּת וְטָעֲתָה עַצְמָהּ וְאָמְרָה, מִכָּל עֵץ הַגָּן נֹאכֵל וּמֵעֵץ הַדַּעַת וְכוּ', אָמַר אֱלֹקִים לֹא תֹאכְלוּ מִמֶּנּוּ וְלֹא תִגְּעוּ בּוֹ וְכוּ', וְהוֹסִיפוּ עַל הַצִּוּוּי. וְתֵכֶף שֶׁהוֹסִיפָה מְעַט עַל הַצִּוּוּי מִיָּד הִצְלִיחַ מַעֲשֵׂה הַסּ"מ כִּי תֵּכֶף עַל-יְדֵי הַהוֹסָפָה יָצְאָה מִן הַמִּדָּה וּבָאָה לִכְלַל בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי אוֹר שֶׁגּוֹרֵם וְכוּ'. וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה דְּחָפָהּ עַד שֶׁנָּגְעָה בּוֹ. וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה בָּאוּ לְמַה שֶּׁבָּאוּ וְהַכֹּל הָיָה רַק עַל-יְדֵי הַהוֹסָפָה שֶׁל הַנָּחָשׁ וְשֶׁל הָאִשָּׁה כַּנַּ"ל. וְכֵן עִקַּר הַחֵטְא הָיָה גַּם כֵּן זֹאת כַּמּוּבָא, כִּי אָדָם הָרִאשׁוֹן הִסְתַּכֵּל לְמַעְלָה מִמַּדְרֵגָתוֹ, שֶׁזֶּה הָיָה עִקַּר הַחֵטְא שֶׁלּוֹ, וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה בָּא לְכָל הַפְּגָמִים שֶׁלּוֹ. וְעַל-כֵּן תֵּכֶף בְּהַתְחָלַת מַתַּן תּוֹרָה הִזְהִיר ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ אֶת מֹשֶׁה כַּמָּה פְּעָמִים, רֵד הָעֵד בָּעָם פֶּן יֶהֶרְסוּ אֶל ה' לַעֲלוֹת וְכוּ'. שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי אוֹר שֶׁבּוֹעֵר לַה' יִתְבָּרַךְ חוּץ מֵהַמִּדָּה, שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת הֲרִיסָה כַּנַּ"ל, כִּי ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ יָדַע מֵחֲמַת גֹּדֶל הִתְגַּלּוּת אֱלֹקוּת שֶׁהָיָה אָז, בְּוַדַּאי יִהְיֶה תַּאֲוָתָם חֲזָקָה מְאֹד לַעֲלוֹת לַה' וּלְהִכָּלֵל בּוֹ בִּתְשׁוּקָה גְּדוֹלָה עַד אֵין סוֹף עַד שֶׁיּוּכְלוּ לָבֹא לִבְחִינַת הֲרִיסָה חַס וְשָׁלוֹם בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי אוֹר, עַל-כֵּן הִזְהִירָם מְאֹד עַל זֶה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתַב רַבֵּנוּ זַ"ל בְּמָקוֹם אַחֵר ((סִימָן עב) שֶׁיֵּשׁ יֵצֶר הָרָע גָּדוֹל כְּשֶׁמַּתְחִילִין לְהִתְקָרֵב לַה' יִתְבָּרַךְ, דְּהַיְנוּ שֶׁהַיֵּצֶר הָרָע מְסִיתוֹ לַהֲרֹס לַעֲלוֹת אֶל ה', שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת פֶּן יֶהֶרְסוּ וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם. וְעַל-כֵּן אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁהָיוּ נִזְהָרִים בְּמִצְוַת הַגְבָּלָה וְלֹא הָרְסוּ לַעֲלוֹת יוֹתֵר, אַף-עַל-פִּי-כֵן מֵחֲמַת שֶׁמַּתַּן תּוֹרָה הָיָה בְּהִתְגַּלּוּת גָּדוֹל בְּקוֹלוֹת וּבְרָקִים וְכוּ' וְכוּ', עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה בָּאוּ אַחַר כָּךְ לְמַה שֶּׁבָּאוּ וְנִכְשְׁלוּ עַל-יְדֵי הָעֵרֶב רַב בִּפְגַם הָעֵגֶל, כְּמוֹ שֶׁפֵּרֵשׁ רַשִׁ"י עַל פָּסוּק, וְאִישׁ לֹא יַעֲלֶה עִמְּךָ. הָרִאשׁוֹנוֹת עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהָיוּ בִּתְשׁוּאוֹת וְהוֹמִיּוֹת, שָׁלְטָה בָּהֶם עַיִן הָרָע, אֵין לְךָ יָפָה מִן הַצְּנִיעוּת, הַיְנוּ כַּנַּ"ל. שֶׁהַלּוּחוֹת הָרִאשׁוֹנוֹת מֵחֲמַת שֶׁהָיָה בְּרַעַשׁ גָּדוֹל וּבְהִתְגַּלּוּת גָּדוֹל מְאֹד מְאֹד, עַל-כֵּן לֹא הָיָה אֶפְשָׁר לְהִתְקַיֵּם כִּי הָיָה בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי אוֹר. וְעַל-כֵּן בָּאוּ לְחֵטְא גָּדוֹל עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה וְנִשְׁבְּרוּ הַלּוּחוֹת, עַל-כֵּן נִתְּנוּ הַשְּׁנִיּוֹת בִּשְׁתִיקָה, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת צִמְצוּם יוֹתֵר, כִּי צְרִיכִין לִזָּהֵר מְאֹד לְצַמְצֵם הָאוֹר בְּהַדְרָגָה וּבְמִדָּה כַּנַּ"ל. וְזֶה בְּחִינַת מַעֲשֵׂה הַמִּשְׁכָּן שֶׁנִּצְטַוּוּ אַחַר מַעֲשֵׂה הָעֵגֶל, כִּי מֵאַחַר שֶׁעִקַּר הַחֵטְא הָיָה עַל-יְדֵי בְּחִינַת רִבּוּי אוֹר כַּנַּ"ל, עַל-כֵּן הֻכְרְחוּ אַחַר כָּךְ לַעֲשׂוֹת הַמִּשְׁכָּן וְכֵלָיו שֶׁכָּלוּל מִגְּוָנִין סַגִּיאִין שֶׁכָּל זֹאת הִיא בְּחִינַת צִמְצוּמִים. לְצַמְצֵם הַמְשָׁכַת הִתְגַּלּוּת אֱלֹקוּתוֹ, כִּי כָּל כְּלִי וּכְלִי וְכָל דָּבָר שֶׁל מַעֲשֵׂה הַמִּשְׁכָּן וּבִגְדֵי כְּהֻנָּה הַכֹּל הָיוּ בְּחִינַת צִמְצוּמִים קְדוֹשִׁים לְקַבֵּל הָאוֹר בְּהַדְרָגָה וּבְמִדָּה, שֶׁזֶּהוּ עִקַּר הַתִּקּוּן כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן בְּכָל עֵת שֶׁנִּצְטַוּוּ עַל מְלֶאכֶת הַמִּשְׁכָּן נִצְטַוּוּ מִקֹּדֶם עַל שַׁבָּת. כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, אֶת שַׁבְּתֹתַי תִּשְׁמֹרוּ וּמִקְדָּשִׁי תִּירָאוּ. כִּי שַׁבָּת הִוא בְּחִינַת הִתְגַּלּוּת אוֹרָיְתָא דְּעַתִּיקָא סְתִימָאָה שֶׁנִּתְגַּלֶּה עַל-יְדֵי תִּקּוּן שֶׁל הַצִּמְצוּם הַנַּ"ל כַּנַּ"ל, שֶׁזֶּהוּ בְּחִינַת מַעֲשֵׂה הַמִּשְׁכָּן כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of the <strong>sin of Adam HaRishon</strong>. For the primary sin was through the aspect of excess light that causes <em>sheviras hakailim</em>, G-d forbid. And therefore the beginning of the Serpent's counsel was through this: that he came to Chavah and said to her, <span class="verse-inline">"Indeed, did G-d say, 'You shall not eat of any tree of the garden'?"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 3:1)</span>. He wanted to mislead her through the "mitzvos" of the <em>yetzer hara</em>, and he asked her whether Hashem's command was not to eat from <em>any</em> tree of the garden — for surely this would be fitting for you, not to eat at all, given the greatness and exaltedness of His, blessed be He — and how could you eat anything at all?!</p>

<p>And because he implanted in them such doubts — that it would be fitting not to eat at all — even though he did not achieve his full intent, he nevertheless achieved something partial. For through this, Chavah responded to him in error, and erred herself, and said, <span class="verse-inline">"Of the fruit of the trees of the garden we may eat, but of the Tree of Knowledge… G-d said, 'You shall not eat of it and you shall not touch it'"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 3:2–3)</span> etc. — and she added to the command. And as soon as she added even a little upon the command, immediately the deed of the <em>Samech Mem</em> <span class="added">[i.e. the Satan]</span> succeeded. For immediately through the addition, she departed from the measured proportion and came to the aspect of excess light that causes etc. And through this he pushed her until she touched it. And through this they came to what they came to — and it was all only through the <strong>addition</strong> of the Serpent and of the woman, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And similarly, the primary sin itself was also this, as is brought — for Adam HaRishon gazed above his level, and this was the essence of his sin, and through this came all his blemishes. Therefore, immediately at the beginning of the giving of the Torah, Hashem warned Moshe several times: <span class="verse-inline">"Go down, warn the people, lest they break through to Hashem to ascend"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Exodus 19:21)</span> etc. — and this is the aspect of excess light, burning for Hashem beyond measure, which is the aspect of breaking-through, as mentioned above. For Hashem knew that because of the great revelation of G-dliness that was occurring then, certainly their desire would be very intense to ascend to Hashem and to be included in Him with longing without end — to the point that they could come to the aspect of breaking-through, G-d forbid, the aspect of excess light. Therefore He warned them greatly about this. As our Rebbe of blessed memory wrote elsewhere (Torah 72): that there is a great <em>yetzer hara</em> when one begins to draw close to Hashem — that is, that the <em>yetzer hara</em> incites him to break through to ascend to Hashem, and this is the aspect of "lest they break through," etc. — see there.</p>

<p>And therefore, even though they were careful with the commandment of the boundary and did not break through to ascend further — nevertheless, because the giving of the Torah was with a great revelation, with thunders and lightnings, etc. — through this they afterwards came to what they came to, and they stumbled through the <em>Airev Rav</em> <span class="added">[the mixed multitude]</span> in the blemish of the <em>Aigel</em> <span class="added">[the golden calf]</span>. As Rashi explained on the verse, <span class="verse-inline">"And no man shall ascend with you"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Exodus 34:3)</span>: the first <span class="added">[tablets]</span>, because they were with clamor and commotion, the evil eye held sway over them — there is nothing finer than modesty. That is, as mentioned above: the first Tablets, because they were with great noise and with an exceedingly great revelation — therefore they could not endure, for it was the aspect of excess light. And therefore they came to a great sin through this, and the Tablets were shattered. Therefore the second <span class="added">[Tablets]</span> were given in silence — and this is the aspect of greater <em>tzimtzum</em>. For one must be very careful to contract the light in gradual stages and in measured proportion, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <strong>construction of the Mishkan</strong> <span class="added">[Tabernacle]</span>, which was commanded after the incident of the <em>Aigel</em>. For since the primary sin was through the aspect of excess light, as mentioned above — therefore they were compelled afterwards to build the Mishkan and its vessels, which comprised many colors <span class="added">[<em>gvanin sagiyin</em>]</span>. For all of this was the aspect of <em>tzimtzumim</em> — to contract the drawing-down of the revelation of His G-dliness. For every vessel and every component of the Mishkan and the priestly garments were all aspects of holy contractions to receive the light in gradual stages and in measured proportion — and this is the primary rectification, as mentioned above. And therefore, every time they were commanded regarding the work of the Mishkan, they were first commanded regarding Shabbos, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"My Sabbaths you shall keep, and My Sanctuary you shall revere"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Leviticus 19:30)</span>. For Shabbos is the aspect of the revelation of <span class="key-term">Oraysa d'Asika Sesima'ah</span> <span class="added">[the Torah of the Hidden Ancient One]</span>, which is revealed through the rectification of the aforementioned <em>tzimtzum</em> — and this is the aspect of the construction of the Mishkan, as mentioned above.</p>

